  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: zookeeper 3.8.3.rhlw-00015",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released org.apache.zookeeper:zookeeper 3.8.3.rhlw-00015 with backported fixes for CVE-2024-23944, CVE-2026-24308, CVE-2026-59739, CVE-2026-59969, CVE-2026-79993, CVE-2026-84439, and CVE-2026-84501.\n\nCVE-2024-23944: Apache ZooKeeper: Information disclosure in persistent watcher handling\n\nCVE-2026-24308: Apache ZooKeeper: Sensitive information disclosure in client configuration handling\n\nCVE-2026-59739: Apache ZooKeeper: Information disclosure via SetWatches reconnect replay\n\nCVE-2026-59969: Apache ZooKeeper: Improper validation of certificate with host mismatch in FIPS mode\n\nCVE-2026-79993: Apache ZooKeeper: Missing ACL check on deleteContainer opcode allows unauthorized deletion of any empty persistent/container znode\n\nCVE-2026-84439: Apache ZooKeeper: Audit log injection via unsanitized output from multiple sources\n\nCVE-2026-84501: Apache ZooKeeper: Operational log forgery via newline injection in EnsembleAuthenticationProvider\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.apache.zookeeper:zookeeper 3.8.3 from Maven Central.",
